# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# Only the single-page fallback belongs here. Pages resolves static assets before
# it reads this file and already answers /jenny with the prerendered jenny.html,
# so naming those routes explicitly is not just redundant — a rule pointing at
# /jenny.html collides with the extension being stripped back to /jenny and the
# two bounce off each other in a redirect loop.
#
# Anything that is not a file falls through to the app, which routes it in the
# browser. A 200, not a redirect, so the URL the visitor arrived on survives.
/*  /index.html  200
